WEBVTT

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.540
Pyeonghwan refers to the endless plains far and wide.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.220
The progress line of Pyeonghwan Pumsae that represents the human will to control the

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:46.300
body and mind, to protect the peaceful plains from domination and pillage, is the character

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:54.520
Il, which means one.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.520
We will now take a look at the key moves of Pyeonghwan Pumsae.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:14.880
Pyeonghwan Pumsae consists of seven key moves, namely Gyeop-seon Jun-bi-ja-sae, Pal-gum-chi

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:29.360
Oryeo-chigi, Go-deul-eol-geul Yeop-mak-gi, Dang-yeo-deung-jumeok Ap-chigi, Mung-ae-chigi,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:39.910
Hae-cheo San-teul-mak-gi, and Mo-ha-seo-gi.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:46.220
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Pyeonghwan Pumsae.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.860
Gyeop-seon Jun-bi-ja-sae is a preparation posture in which both arms straighten from

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.260
Mo-ha-seo-gi.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:59.940
The left hand is placed over the back of the right hand in the shape of a cross.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.740
The hands should be slightly apart from the body in front of the lower abdomen

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.980
with the palm of the left hand placed over the back of the right hand in the

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.140
shape of a cross.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:19.020
Prepare the fingertips of both hands together and your fingers should not be spread apart.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:29.380
Par-gum-chi Oryeo-chigi is a technique to strike upward using the elbow.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:34.700
The basic target is an opponent's chin, but it can also be used to strike the solar

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.940
plexus, chest, and other areas.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.660
When performing the move, make sufficient use of the twisting of your torso with

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.180
your elbow close to your body.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.380
Raise your fist to reduce resistance from your muscles and maintain a sufficient

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.780
range of movement.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:58.600
Be careful not to strengthen the arm to strike upward.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.760
Go-do-ro-ol-gul-yeop-mak-gi

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:06.660
Starts with the Chagin-dol-jogui posture.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:11.100
The blocking arm should pass the face and the elbow and placed to your side

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.300
level with your philtrum.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:17.780
Your elbow should straighten and be perpendicular to the ground.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:22.140
The assisting arm should be parallel to the ground at chest height.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:27.700
And the space between your body and arm should be about one raised fist length.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:32.020
The fist on the assisting arm should not move outside the body.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:38.050
The blocking arm should not tilt front, back, left, right.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:42.530
Dangyeo-deung-joo-mok-ap-chigi is a technique to pull an opponent with one

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:48.090
hand and strike their face in the philtrum or chin forward from the inside

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.810
using the other back fist.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:57.090
It can also be used to attack other areas depending on the situation.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:00.610
The back fist is placed in front of the philtrum.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:07.020
And it should not be a strike from the outside in like Me-joo-mok-an-chigi.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:14.980
Mong-ae-chigi is a technique used to attack both sides using the elbow

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:20.260
by crossing your arms above and below in front of the chest.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:24.860
Your back fist must face upward, and the back of your two hammer fists should

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.780
lightly touch your chest.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:33.250
Your arms must be parallel.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:38.210
When performing mong-ae-chigi, be careful not to let your elbows move back

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:43.910
and make sure your chest does not open.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:51.430
Hae-choo-san-teul-mak-i is a technique where your arms cross at the lower abdomen

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:56.990
and move your sides horizontally in front of your face to perform ol-geul-hae-choo-mak-i

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:59.950
with your inner wrist.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:06.450
Your arms should be at the philtrum level and perpendicular to the ground.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:11.890
Be careful not to let the wrist bend and the blocking arm must not tilt front, back,

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.700
left, right.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:19.640
Mo-ha-seo-gi is a posture where the back of the foot blades are adjacent to

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.360
and the knees are straightened and aligned to the center line.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:32.240
Your eyes should be directed forward and be careful not to let space exist between your feet.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:38.310
These are the 7 key moves of pyeong-won-poom-se.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:46.810
We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.690
The key moves of pyeong-won first part consist of

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:58.060
kyeop-seong-joon-bi

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:03.490
ar-ae-hae-choo-mak-i

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:10.630
tong-mil-gi

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:15.810
and or-un-sol-nal-ar-ae-mak-i.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:22.670
There are no cautions you should be aware of in pyeong-won first part.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:52.080
We will now practice the moves of pyeong-won first part in succession while watching the video.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.720
The key moves of pyeong-won second part consist of

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.880
wen-sol-nal-pak-at-mak-i

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.880
or-un-pal-koon-chi-eol-yeo-chig-i

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.240
or-un-ap-cha-gi

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:08.680
wen-fu-t-mo-m-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:11.720
or-un-sol-nal-go-do-ro-mak-i

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.360
or-un-sol-nal-go-do-ro-ar-ae-mak-i

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:20.280
and or-un-an-pal-mok-go-do-ro-ol-geul-yeop-mak-i.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.360
When performing wen-sol-nal-pak-at-mak-i,

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.480
move your center to the right foot

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.640
and at the same time twist the heel backward

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:32.600
and set your left foot a bit to the outside

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:36.240
and perform or-un-dwik-gu-bi-sol-nal-pak-at-mak-i.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.440
When performing or-un-pal-koon-chi-eol-yeo-chig-i,

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.160
set your left foot forward about one and a half steps

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.240
then perform pal-koon-chi-eol-yeo-chig-i.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.960
Your left ball should touch the ground first

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.640
then finish the move along with a breath

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.920
the moment your heel touches the ground.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.560
When performing ap-cha-gi,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.240
the heel of the supporting foot

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.800
should not twist inward excessively.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.200
If the foot is twisted excessively inward,

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.760
the force is dispersed,

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:08.040
weakens the force transferred forward

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.160
or results in loss of balance.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.960
When performing mung-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi,

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.800
the right leg that kicked forward

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.880
should pass the left foot slightly

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.320
and set so the ball touches the ground.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.720
The heel of the foot that kicked forward

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:26.360
should point in the direction of the kick.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:29.160
Next, move your center to the right leg

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.960
to create a central axis.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.600
Pass the left foot over the right knee.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.720
Turn the upper body toward the direction of the kick

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.440
then perform yeop-cha-gi.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.960
Ap-cha-gi followed by mung-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:47.160
must connect naturally in a skillful manner.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.600
You may lose balance if the kicking foot moves

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:53.920
too far away from the supporting foot.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.480
If the hips fall back

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.960
or the heel of the supporting foot fall back

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:00.400
rather than point in the direction of the kick

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.240
when performing yeop-cha-gi,

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.880
the force transferred forward weakens

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.200
or the balance may be disrupted.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.760
Pay attention to the direction

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:12.080
the heel of the supporting foot points toward.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.760
After performing mung-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi,

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.240
bend your knee and raise the upper body

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:20.720
at the same time to perform son-na-go-do-ra-ma-ki.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.480
Connect all the moves from orun-ap-cha-gi

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:26.280
to mung-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:31.710
and son-na-go-do-ro-ma-ki without disconnect.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:34.270
When performing orun-son-na-go-do-ro-ma-ki,

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:38.590
draw a big circle over your head with your arms,

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:41.190
then perform son-na-go-do-ro-are-ma-ki.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:46.070
When performing orun-an-pal-mo-go-do-ro-ol-gu-yeop-ma-ki,

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:47.670
raise the right foot slightly

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.870
from the wen-di-ku-bi posture.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.950
Set it as parallel to the left foot on the ground,

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:56.580
then block.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.060
Cautions for pyeong-won second part,

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.500
taking a closer look.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:03.620
Move and set your left foot

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:08.140
when performing wen-son-na-pa-kal-ma-ki.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.820
When transitioning from di-ku-bi to ap-ku-bi posture

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.420
during orun-pal-gu-p-o-ryo-chi-gi,

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:15.980
be careful not to let your feet

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.740
completely touch the ground at the same time.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:22.580
When performing mung-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi,

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:29.210
be mindful that the move shouldn't halt.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:31.170
The foot performing the yeop-cha-gi

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:34.490
should not pass under the knee of the supporting leg.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.530
Do a folding kick.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:39.170
When performing son-na-go-do-ro-are-ma-ki,

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.370
during son-na-go-do-ro-ma-ki,

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:44.650
the position of your head must not change.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:48.530
When performing orun-an-pal-mo-go-do-ro-ol-gu-yeop-ma-ki,

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:51.970
the assisting fist should not move outside the body.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:57.390
Be careful not to let the blocking arm tilt.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:12:00.390
We will now practice the moves of pyeong-won second part

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:18.300
in succession while watching the video.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.900
The key moves of pyeong-won third part consist of

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:24.140
dang-yeo-deung-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:28.260
Dang-yeo-deung-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.840
Mung-ae-chi-gi.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.440
Hae-cheo-san-teul-ma-ki.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.450
Geum-gang-ma-ki.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.090
Wen-cha-geun-do-jeo-gui.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.720
Orun-yeop-cha-gi.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:46.880
Wen-pal-kum-chi-o-ryo-chi-gi.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:51.310
Wen-ap-cha-gi.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.710
Orun-fut-mo-do-ra-yeop-cha-gi.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.030
Wen-son-nal-go-do-ro-ma-ki.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.270
Wen-son-nal-go-do-ro-are-ma-ki.

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:06.800
And Wen-an-pal-mok-go-do-ro-ol-gu-yeop-ma-ki.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:13.160
We will explain the dang-yeo-deung-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi move first.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:15.640
First, open the right hand

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.080
and naturally straighten the arm forward.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:22.000
Then pull the right fist along with the torso

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:26.080
and move the right foot so it touches the left knee.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.240
This is a preparatory posture

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.600
to dodge an opponent's attack of the lower body

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.160
and repeat the chi-chi-gi attack.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:38.800
All these moves must be performed simultaneously.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.920
Remember the moves explained previously.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:46.560
Perform the preparatory moves.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.080
When the preparatory move is complete,

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:55.680
pull the right hand and connect with deung-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.480
Pull an opponent with the left hand.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.880
At the same time, perform chi-chi-gi

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.880
with the right foot and attack your opponent's face

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.920
with the back of your right fist.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:09.000
Shout at this time

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.040
and let your right elbow lightly touch

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:13.480
the back of your left hand from above.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.400
When performing dang-yeo-deung-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.880
with the left hand, pull the left hand back.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.360
Lightly straighten the right fist forward

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.920
and at the same time, pull back.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:30.280
Strike an opponent's face with the back of your left fist.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:33.680
Do not perform chi-chi-gi at this point.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.600
For mung-ae-chi-gi, perform go-ah-seo-gi

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.160
by crossing your left foot in front of your right foot.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.400
Cross your left arm over your right arm

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.880
in front of your chest,

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:46.520
then strike both sides with your elbows.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:55.960
Pull your right foot while performing geum-gang-mak-gi.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:15:00.400
Tageun-do-jeo-gui is a move connected to geum-gang-mak-gi.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.320
Elevation of the stance should be maintained.

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:08.050
Your eyes should point in the direction of progress.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.570
O-reun-yeop-ja-gi is performed from hak-da-ri-seo-gi

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:15.930
while maintaining tageun-do-jeo-gui.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:21.630
When performing wen-pal-gum-chi-oh-ryo-chi-gi,

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:23.190
complete the move the moment

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:28.270
the right heel touches the ground.

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:32.070
When performing o-reun-foot-mo-m-do-ra-yeop-ja-gi,

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:35.190
the left kicking foot passes the right foot slightly

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.710
and set with the ball touching the ground.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:41.350
The heel of the kicking foot points in the direction

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:42.510
of the kick.

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:44.510
Move your center to the left foot

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.470
and create a central axis.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.670
Move the right foot past the left knee.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.630
Turn your upper body in the direction of the kick,

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.350
then perform yeop-ja-gi.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.950
Ap-ja-gi and mo-m-do-ra-yeop-ja-gi

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.990
should be performed in succession.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:04.670
After mo-m-do-ra-yeop-ja-gi,

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.670
fold the knee of the kicking leg

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.270
while raising your upper body

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:13.550
to connect to son-nal-go-do-ro-mak-gi.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:17.190
When performing son-nal-go-do-ro-are-mak-gi,

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.670
complete the move by drawing a big circle

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:24.330
above your head with your arms.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.050
The wen-go-do-ro-ol-gu-yeop-mak-gi

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:29.970
is completed by raising the left foot slightly

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:31.810
from the o-reun-di-ku-bi

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:36.370
and setting it parallel with the right foot.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:39.010
Cautions for pyeong-won third part,

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:42.320
taking a closer look.

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:45.440
When performing dang-gyeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi,

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.640
the assisting knee should not bend.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.920
Be careful not to let it move outside,

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:57.030
like mae-ju-mok-an-chi-gi.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.830
When performing dang-gyeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.310
with the left hand,

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.190
do not perform jjit-jjik-gi

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:08.440
and do not open your hand.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.800
Do not perform geum-gang-mak-gi slowly.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.960
When performing jjageun-do-jeok-ui,

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.520
pay attention to maintaining your balance.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:20.080
Ap-ja-gi and mo-m-do-ra-yeop-ja-gi,

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.600
son-nal-go-do-ro-mo-m-do-mak-gi

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:26.730
should all be performed in succession.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:30.010
As already mentioned in pyeong-won second part,

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:32.330
the position of the head must not change

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:35.010
when performing son-nal-go-do-ro-arae-mak-gi

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.570
during the son-nal-go-do-ro-mak-gi move.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:43.250
When performing an-pal-mok-go-do-ro-ol-gu-yeop-mak-gi,

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:47.010
the fist of the assisting arm must move outside the body.

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:51.680
The blocking arm should not tilt.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.840
We will now practice the moves of pyeong-won third part

00:17:54.840 --> 00:18:19.280
in succession while watching the video.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.880
The key moves of pyeong-won fourth part consist of

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:26.120
dang-yeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.160
dang-yeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.800
mung-ae-chi-gi

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:35.360
hae-cho-san-deul-mak-gi

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:38.550
geum-gang-mak-gi

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:41.230
oran-ja-geun-do-jeok-ui

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:43.350
wen-yeop-ja-gi

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:50.140
and oran-pal-koon-chi-pyo-jeok-chi-gi

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.900
As we did for the first move of pyeong-won third part,

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.260
we will first explain the preparatory move

00:18:56.260 --> 00:19:01.080
for the dang-yeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:06.730
Open your right hand and naturally straighten your arm.

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:09.530
Pull your left fist back along the torso

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:15.350
and slightly touch your right knee with your left foot.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:20.340
All these moves should be performed simultaneously.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.660
Let's now perform the preparatory move

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:25.180
we previously explained independently.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:30.740
When performing dang-yeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi,

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:32.700
pull the left arm back,

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:36.100
lightly open the right fist moving forward

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:41.580
while striking the opponent's face with the left back fist.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:45.480
When performing dang-yeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:48.880
with the right hand afterwards,

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:51.280
pull the right arm back

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.080
and lightly straighten the left fist

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.720
moving forward while striking an opponent's face

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:00.920
with the right back fist.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:04.880
Do not perform jit-jit-gi at this time.

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:06.280
For mung-ae-chi-gi,

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:09.040
perform go-ah-seo-gi by crossing your right foot

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.920
in front of your left foot.

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:14.320
Cross your right arm over the left in front of your chest,

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:18.240
then strike both sides with your elbows.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.720
Pull the left foot and at the same time

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:26.050
perform geum-gang-mak-gi.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:30.370
Jageun-do-jeo-gui is a move connected to geum-gang-mak-gi.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.890
Maintain your stance

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:37.790
and your eyes should point in the direction of progress.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:39.790
Then connect to wen-yeop-ja-gi

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.790
while maintaining jageun-do-jeo-gui

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:43.790
in the hak-dal-i-seo-gi posture.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.830
For the following move,

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:48.270
keep your left arm straight

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:51.430
as if performing mae-ju-mok-bak-ga-chi-gi

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:57.240
and keep your arm and leg in a parallel alignment.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:00.920
When performing eoreun-pal-gum-chi-pyo-jeok-chi-gi,

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.840
twist your upper body about 45 degrees

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:09.930
and strike the palm of your left hand with your right elbow.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:13.650
Your target should level with the solar plexus

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:19.530
and you should utilize the torque of your torso as much as possible.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:23.530
When performing pal-gum-chi-pyo-jeok-chi-gi at the torso level,

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:25.850
it should take the form of a raised fist

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:30.650
in order to minimize stress on muscles and tension in the shoulders,

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:33.690
making it possible to strike fast and hard

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:39.560
and making sufficient use of the upper body's range of movement.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:42.160
Cautions for Byung-won 4th part.

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.510
Taking a closer look.

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.510
When performing a preparatory move

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:49.990
for dang-gyeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi,

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.990
do not bend the knee of the supporting leg.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:56.790
When performing dang-gyeo-doong-ju-mok-ap-chi-gi,

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:02.130
do not perform mae-ju-mok-an-chi-gi outside in.

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.850
When performing eoreun-dang-gyeo-ap-chi-gi,

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:08.370
do not perform mae-ju-mok-an-chi-gi outside in

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:13.240
and be careful not to open the hand.

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:18.280
Do not perform jit-jik-gi at this point.

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:20.480
When performing jageun-dol-jeok-ui,

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:22.880
pay attention to maintaining your balance

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:29.160
and quickly perform geum-gang-mak-gi.

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:31.160
When performing wen-yeop-chagi,

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:35.360
do not kick with the upper body below the back.

00:22:35.360 --> 00:22:40.910
Also, be careful not to let your hips fall backwards.

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:44.230
When performing eoreun-pal-gum-chi-pyo-jok-chigi,

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:52.740
excessive twisting of the back may cause you to lose balance.

00:22:52.740 --> 00:22:54.220
Concentrate on the moves

00:22:54.220 --> 00:23:00.020
so you do not perform pal-gup-chigi on your fingers.

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:04.020
We will now practice the moves of pyeong-won 4th part in succession

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:20.780
while watching the video.

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:24.540
This concludes the training for pyeong-won pum-se.

00:23:24.540 --> 00:24:34.260
We will take another look at the moves and master pum-se.

00:24:34.260 --> 00:24:37.060
We have looked at the key moves of pyeong-won pum-se

00:24:37.060 --> 00:24:39.860
and provided thorough explanations for each move

00:24:39.860 --> 00:24:41.860
and things to watch out for.

00:24:41.860 --> 00:24:43.780
I hope this was a good opportunity

00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:46.780
for a reminder of the far and wide plains

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:48.180
and the spirit of struggle

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:51.580
to protect the peaceful foundations of life.

00:24:51.580 --> 00:24:55.180
We will see you again in the shib-jin pum-se video.

00:24:55.180 --> 00:24:56.460
Thanks for watching.

